{
    "chapter_num": 3,
    "verses_count": 18,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "The Untamable Tongue"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "My brethren, let not many of you become teachers, knowing that we shall receive a stricter judgment. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "For we all stumble in many things. If anyone does not stumble in word, he "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " a "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "mature"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "perfect man, able also to bridle the whole body. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "NU Now if"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Indeed, we put bits in horses’ mouths that they may obey us, and we turn their whole body. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Look also at ships: although they are so large and are driven by fierce winds, they are turned by a very small rudder wherever the pilot desires. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Even so the tongue is a little member and boasts great things."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "See how great a forest a little fire kindles! "
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And the tongue "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " a fire, a world of "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "unrighteousness"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "iniquity. The tongue is so set among our members that it defiles the whole body, and sets on fire the course of "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "existence"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "nature; and it is set on fire by "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Gr. Gehenna"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "hell. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "For every kind of beast and bird, of reptile and creature of the sea, is tamed and has been tamed by mankind. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 8,
                    "num_str": "8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But no man can tame the tongue. "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "It is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " an unruly evil, full of deadly poison. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 9,
                    "num_str": "9",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "With it we bless our God and Father, and with it we curse men, who have been made in the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "likeness"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "similitude of God. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 10,
                    "num_str": "10",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Out of the same mouth proceed blessing and cursing. My brethren, these things ought not to be so. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 11,
                    "num_str": "11",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Does a spring send forth fresh "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "water"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " and bitter from the same opening? "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 12,
                    "num_str": "12",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Can a fig tree, my brethren, bear olives, or a grapevine bear figs? "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "NU Neither can a salty spring produce fresh water."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Thus no spring yields both salt water and fresh."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Heavenly Versus Demonic Wisdom"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 13,
                    "num_str": "13",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Who "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " wise and understanding among you? Let him show by good conduct "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "that"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " his works "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "are done"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " in the meekness of wisdom. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 14,
                    "num_str": "14",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But if you have bitter envy and "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "selfish ambition"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "self-seeking in your hearts, do not boast and lie against the truth. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 15,
                    "num_str": "15",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "This wisdom does not descend from above, but "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " earthly, sensual, demonic. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 16,
                    "num_str": "16",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "For where envy and self-seeking "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "exist,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " confusion and every evil thing "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "are"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " there. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 17,
                    "num_str": "17",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But the wisdom that is from above is first pure, then peaceable, gentle, willing to yield, full of mercy and good fruits, without partiality and without hypocrisy. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 18,
                    "num_str": "18",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now the fruit of righteousness is sown in peace by those who make peace."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}